['greece-dolmades','Dolmades (Greek Rice and Herb Stuffed Vine Leaves)','Greece','🇬🇷',60,['vine leaves','rice','onion','dill','mint','lemon','olive oil'],[[18,'piece'],[70,'g'],[60,'g'],[8,'g'],[5,'g'],[0.5,'piece'],[1.5,'tbsp']],'https://www.visitgreece.gr/en/experiences/culture/local-traditions/kalymnos-gastronomy',['Rinse the vine leaves and blanch briefly if they are fresh; drain and cool.','Soften onion in half the oil, add rice and herbs, and cook for two minutes.','Place a teaspoon of filling on each leaf, fold the sides in, and roll snugly.','Arrange seam-side down, add 220 ml water, lemon, and remaining oil, then simmer covered until tender.']],
['greece-stifado','Stifado (Greek Beef and Pearl Onion Stew)','Greece','🇬🇷',110,['beef chuck','pearl onion','tomato','red wine','olive oil','cinnamon','bay leaf'],[[180,'g'],[180,'g'],[140,'g'],[80,'ml'],[1,'tbsp'],[0.25,'tsp'],[1,'piece']],'https://www.visitgreece.gr/experiences/gastronomy/traditional-cuisine/local-flavours-of-the-greek-cuisine/',['Brown the beef in olive oil, remove it, and lightly colour the peeled pearl onions.','Return the beef and add tomato, wine, cinnamon, bay leaf, and 120 ml water.','Cover and simmer gently until the beef is tender and safely cooked.','Uncover to thicken the sauce while keeping the onions intact, then rest briefly before serving.']],
['greece-revithada','Revithada (Sifnos Slow-Baked Chickpea Stew)','Greece','🇬🇷',120,['cooked chickpeas','onion','olive oil','lemon','bay leaf','oregano','water'],[[240,'g'],[90,'g'],[1.5,'tbsp'],[0.5,'piece'],[1,'piece'],[0.5,'tsp'],[220,'ml']],'https://www.visitgreece.gr/en/experiences/gastronomy/traditional-cuisine/the-gastronomy-of-sifnos',['Place cooked chickpeas and thinly sliced onion in a small lidded casserole.','Add olive oil, bay leaf, oregano, water, and a small pinch of salt.','Cover tightly and bake at 160°C until the chickpeas are creamy and the liquid is rich.','Remove the bay leaf, brighten with lemon juice, and serve warm.']],
['greece-galaktoboureko','Galaktoboureko (Greek Semolina Custard Filo Pie)','Greece','🇬🇷',70,['filo pastry','milk','semolina','egg','sugar','butter','lemon'],[[90,'g'],[250,'ml'],[30,'g'],[1,'piece'],[45,'g'],[25,'g'],[0.5,'piece']],'https://www.visitgreece.gr/en/experiences/architecture/local-architecture/galaktoboureko',['Whisk milk, semolina, egg, 20 g sugar, and lemon zest over low heat until thick.','Brush a small dish with butter and layer in two-thirds of the filo, buttering each sheet.','Add the cooled custard, fold over the edges, and cover with the remaining buttered filo.','Bake at 180°C until crisp; spoon over a light syrup made with remaining sugar, lemon, and 35 ml water.']],
['greece-bougatsa','Bougatsa Thessalonikis (Greek Custard Filo Pastry)','Greece','🇬🇷',50,['filo pastry','milk','semolina','sugar','butter','vanilla','cinnamon'],[[85,'g'],[230,'ml'],[28,'g'],[35,'g'],[25,'g'],[0.25,'tsp'],[0.25,'tsp']],'https://www.visitgreece.gr/en/experiences/gastronomy/greek-wines/thessaloniki-a-culinary-paradise',['Heat milk with sugar and semolina, whisking until a smooth custard forms; add vanilla and cool.','Layer buttered filo in a small baking dish, leaving enough pastry to fold over the filling.','Spread in the custard, close the filo, and brush the top with remaining butter.','Bake at 190°C until deeply golden, then dust lightly with cinnamon before serving.']],
['greece-soutzoukakia','Soutzoukakia Smyrneika (Cumin Meatballs in Tomato Sauce)','Greece','🇬🇷',45,['ground beef','bread crumbs','garlic','cumin','tomato','olive oil','rice'],[[160,'g'],[25,'g'],[1,'clove'],[0.75,'tsp'],[180,'g'],[1,'tbsp'],[70,'g']],'https://www.visitgreece.gr/en/experiences/leisure/shopping/gastronomy-of-komotini',['Mix beef, breadcrumbs, garlic, cumin, salt, and 20 ml water; shape into small oblong meatballs.','Brown the meatballs in half the olive oil, then remove them from the pan.','Cook tomato in the remaining oil, return the meatballs, and simmer until safely cooked.','Boil the rice separately and serve it with the meatballs and cumin-scented sauce.']],
['greece-dakos','Dakos (Cretan Barley Rusk, Tomato, and Cheese Salad)','Greece','🇬🇷',15,['barley rusk','tomato','feta cheese','olive oil','oregano','olives','red wine vinegar'],[[80,'g'],[170,'g'],[60,'g'],[1,'tbsp'],[0.5,'tsp'],[25,'g'],[1,'tsp']],'https://www.discovergreece.com/travel-ideas/cover-story/foodie-guide-crete',['Sprinkle the barley rusk with two tablespoons of water so it softens without becoming soggy.','Grate or finely chop the tomato and season it with vinegar and a small pinch of salt.','Spoon the tomato over the rusk and crumble the feta on top.','Finish with olives, oregano, and olive oil and serve immediately.']],
['greece-loukoumades','Loukoumades (Greek Honey and Cinnamon Dough Puffs)','Greece','🇬🇷',50,['flour','water','dry yeast','sugar','cooking oil','honey','cinnamon'],[[100,'g'],[95,'ml'],[2,'g'],[5,'g'],[250,'ml'],[1.5,'tbsp'],[0.25,'tsp']],'https://www.visitgreece.gr/en/experiences/leisure/shopping/loukoumades',['Mix flour, yeast, sugar, water, and a pinch of salt into a thick smooth batter.','Cover and let the batter rise until visibly bubbly and almost doubled.','Drop teaspoon portions into 175°C oil and fry until evenly golden; drain well.','Drizzle the warm puffs with honey and sprinkle with cinnamon.']],
['greece-shrimp-saganaki','Garides Saganaki (Greek Shrimp with Tomato and Feta)','Greece','🇬🇷',30,['shrimp','tomato','feta cheese','onion','garlic','olive oil','oregano'],[[180,'g'],[180,'g'],[55,'g'],[50,'g'],[1,'clove'],[1,'tbsp'],[0.5,'tsp']],'https://www.visitgreece.gr/en/experiences/architecture/traditional-settlements/cuisine-of-lesvos',['Soften onion and garlic in olive oil without letting the garlic burn.','Add tomato and oregano and simmer until the sauce becomes concentrated.','Add shrimp and cook only until opaque and safely cooked through.','Crumble feta over the pan, warm briefly without overcooking the shrimp, and serve.']],
['greece-skordalia','Skordalia (Greek Garlic, Potato, and Olive Oil Dip)','Greece','🇬🇷',30,['potato','garlic','olive oil','red wine vinegar','lemon','salt'],[[220,'g'],[2,'clove'],[2,'tbsp'],[1,'tsp'],[0.25,'piece'],[1,'g']],'https://www.visitgreece.gr/experiences/gastronomy/traditional-cuisine/local-flavours-of-the-greek-cuisine/',['Boil the peeled potato in lightly salted water until completely tender, then drain well.','Pound the garlic with salt into a smooth paste.','Mash the hot potato and gradually beat in garlic paste, olive oil, and vinegar.','Adjust with lemon juice and a spoonful of cooking water until creamy, then cool slightly.']]
